body:
For our users to be able to build things like "hide the hits widget when the query is empty", we could just forward the helper events to the instantsearch instance.

So that the user could:

``` js
search.on('change', function(state) {
  if (state.query === '') {
    hits.classList.add('hide');
  }

  // hits being the hits container you have a reference to already (from your code)
});
```

cc @proudlygeek what do you think?

